Read: if the 1024-thread rows report tg/core = 1.00 at every tgmem
setting including the smallest, then the concurrent-thread budget is the
binding constraint and no threadgroup-memory reduction can raise
occupancy.  If tg/core rises as tgmem falls, threadgroup memory is the
binding constraint and a smaller threadgroup allocation buys occupancy.
